# What `gcloud builds submit` / `gcloud run deploy --source .` uploads.
#
# Without this file gcloud uploads the whole working tree. `data/` is 2.8 GB of
# SQLite index; uploading it would cost minutes per deploy and land another copy
# in gs://dynamics-mcp_cloudbuild/source/ every time.
#
# EVERY directory pattern here is anchored with a leading slash. This file uses
# gitignore semantics, where a bare `metadata/` matches at ANY depth — which
# silently excluded src/metadata/, src/bridge/ and src/eval/ from the upload and
# broke the build with ~120 "Cannot find module" errors that looked like a
# TypeScript problem. Anchor or it bites again.
#
# Keep in sync with .dockerignore — this controls the upload, that controls the
# image layer. An entry missing here is a slow deploy; missing there is a fat
# image.
/data/
/extracted-metadata/
/metadata/
/instances/
/dist/
/coverage/
/tmp/

# Windows-only C# bridge — not used by the read-only cloud image. Anchored, so
# src/bridge/ (TypeScript, required to compile) is still uploaded.
/bridge/

# Root-level only: src/eval/ is part of the compile and must ship.
/tests/
/eval/
/docs/

/.git/
/.github/
/.azure-pipelines/
/.claude/
/.vscode/
/.idea/

# node_modules is intentionally unanchored — nested copies are just as unwanted.
node_modules/

*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo

.env
.env.*
.mcp.json
/config/d365fo-mcp.json
/config/secrets.json
deployment.zip
